 /*
  * ps3recomp - cellUsbd HLE implementation
  *
- * Stub. Init/term work, no USB devices are enumerated.
- * Games that require specific USB peripherals will need
- * proper device emulation.
+ * See cellUsbd.h. With no steering wheel on the PC (or PS3_WHEEL=off) this is
+ * what it always was: Init/End succeed and the bus stays empty.
+ *
+ * With a wheel, one emulated Logitech G27 (dev_id 1) sits on the bus. A worker
+ * thread plays libusbd's part: once a game driver is registered for 046D:C29B
+ * it calls the driver's probe and attach, answers its control transfers
+ * (standard requests; HID SET_REPORT goes to the force-feedback decoder),
+ * takes its interrupt OUT writes (force feedback), and completes its interrupt
+ * IN reads with the wheel's current report -- when the report changes, at most
+ * every 2 ms (the G27's bInterval), and every 8 ms regardless. Unplugging the
+ * PC wheel detaches the G27 and plugging it back attaches it again.
+ *
+ * Every callback into the game runs on the worker, never inside the call that
+ * queued the transfer: GT5's attach queues SET_CONFIGURATION and expects to
+ * finish attaching before the completion arrives, as on the console.
+ *
+ * GT5's callbacks only post an event to its USB thread's queue (40 events),
+ * and that thread queues the next read once it has handled a report. On a
+ * small PC at full load the thread falls behind, the queue fills with
+ * force-feedback completions, and a report's event can be dropped: the game
+ * then never asks for another and keeps the last one, the car steering and
+ * accelerating (or braking) on its own. So only one report at a time waits
+ * to be taken, and one not taken in 1.5 s goes again (a player's laptop at
+ * 20 fps, 15 Nov 2026; seen here with PS3_WHEEL=virtual, jitter=1 on four
+ * E-cores). PS3_WHEEL_TRACE=1 logs counts every 10 s.
+ *
+ * GT5 (BCES00569) walk-through, for the next person: probe 0xC21588 checks the
+ * device descriptor's VID:PID; attach 0xC21878 scans config/interface/endpoint
+ * descriptors, opens the control and both interrupt pipes, registers a custom
+ * pad (cellPadLddRegisterController) and sends SET_CONFIGURATION; its USB
+ * event thread (0xC20DC0) then starts the IN reads, decodes each report
+ * (0xC1EA58) into the custom pad and the game's wheel state, and sends force
+ * feedback through 0xC208E0 / 0xC20890. Those addresses are the EU build's;
+ * GT5 01.04 (BCUS98114) checks 046D:C298-C29B in func_00C5E154.
+ *
+ * Adapted from gt5-recomp (https://github.com/MormonFTP-hub/gt5-recomp),
+ * MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 MormonFTP-hub.
+ * Here the descriptor page comes from the runtime's scratch allocator instead
+ * of a fixed page of the HLE inject window.
  */
 
